</style>
<small>shape: (3, 5)</small><table border="1" class="dataframe"><thead><tr><th>species</th><th>islands</th><th>masses</th><th>n_islands</th><th>mass_max</th></tr><tr><td>str</td><td>list[str]</td><td>list[i64]</td><td>u32</td><td>i64</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&quot;Adelie&quot;</td><td>[&quot;Biscoe&quot;, &quot;Dream&quot;, &quot;Torgersen&quot;]</td><td>[3750, 3800, … 4000]</td><td>3</td><td>4775</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Gentoo&quot;</td><td>[&quot;Biscoe&quot;]</td><td>[4500, 5700, … 5400]</td><td>1</td><td>6300</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Chinstrap&quot;</td><td>[&quot;Dream&quot;]</td><td>[3500, 3900, … 3775]</td><td>1</td><td>4800</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
```
:::
:::


`pl.concat_list()` / `pl.concat_arr()` pack a row into a List / Array (≈
`c_across()`), `pl.struct()` into a Struct (≈ `pick()`), and `implode()` packs
a whole column (or, with `.over()`, a group) into one cell:

::: {#bff1894d .cell execution_count=4}
``` {.python .cell-code}
penguins_df.head(2).select(
    as_list=pl.concat_list("bill_length_mm", "bill_depth_mm"),
    as_array=pl.concat_arr("bill_length_mm", "bill_depth_mm"),
    as_struct=pl.struct("bill_length_mm", "bill_depth_mm"),
    all_years=pl.col("year").implode(),
)
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}
```{=html}
